# Input rail definitions (Colang format)
# Blocks harmful, off-topic, or jailbreak prompts before they reach the LLM.
# Implementation: Part 5
#
# NOTE: guardrails/manager.py's GuardrailsManager invokes the self_check_input
# action directly via the action dispatcher, bypassing this flow entirely, for
# speed and to avoid pulling in the full Colang dialog-flow engine (see
# docs/tradeoffs.md). This flow is kept as the canonical, human-readable
# definition of the intended behavior, and works unchanged if a future part
# switches to driving guardrails through rails.generate()/Colang directly.

define flow check harmful input
  $allowed = execute self_check_input

  if not $allowed
    bot refuse input
    stop

define bot refuse input
  "I'm not able to help with that. Let's talk about something else."
